=== C0 Drude: J(w) = g0 w k^2/(w^2+k^2)  ->  gamma(t) = (2/pi) int_0^inf J(w)/w cos(wt) dw ===
  gamma(t) = gamma0*kappa*exp(-kappa*t)  (exponential = P-06b p=1 edge; classical noise C_F = T gamma by FDT)
  T/kappa=5.00: negative Bernstein weights: none;  C_sym(t=0.5,2,5,10) = +3.023e+00, +6.744e-01, +3.358e-02, +2.262e-04 -> CM (all weights > 0)
  T/kappa=0.30: negative Bernstein weights: ['c0'];  C_sym(t=0.5,2,5,10) = +1.787e-01, +3.798e-03, -2.882e-04, -2.180e-06 -> NOT CM
  T/kappa=0.05: negative Bernstein weights: [1, 2, 3];  C_sym(t=0.5,2,5,10) = +1.056e-01, -4.666e-02, -1.366e-02, -1.732e-03 -> NOT CM
  classical limit (T >> kappa): C_sym -> T gamma(t), CM;  low T (nu_1 = 2 pi T < kappa): Matsubara weights turn negative -> quantum noise kernel NOT CM though gamma(t) is exactly exponential

=== C1 pathwise identity: autonomous Hamiltonian bath  ==  GLE with free-bath force F (one microstate) ===
  Drude (CM edge)            max|q_H - q_GLE| on [0,6.0] = 5.34e-06  (|q| <= 1.05; GLE dt=1e-03, O(dt^2))
  two-exponential (CM)       max|q_H - q_GLE| on [0,6.0] = 1.41e-06  (|q| <= 1.00; GLE dt=1e-03, O(dt^2))
  resonant (non-CM)          max|q_H - q_GLE| on [0,6.0] = 4.06e-06  (|q| <= 1.03; GLE dt=1e-03, O(dt^2))
  deterministic microstate: q_H(t) is a fixed trajectory; the 'exogenous' match is the Dirac law on that F path

